PURPOSE:
Bitwise deterministic simulation engine.

FORMAL MODEL:

    S(t+1) = Ξ(S(t), I(t))

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUST REFERENCE CORE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub fn tick(&mut self) {
    for i in 0..self.entities.len() {
        self.pos[i].0 += self.vel[i].0 * DT;
        self.pos[i].1 += self.vel[i].1 * DT;
        self.pos[i].2 += self.vel[i].2 * DT;
    }
}
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INVARIANT GUARANTEE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- No floating-point nondeterminism
- No thread-order dependence
- Identical execution across CPU / SIMD / WASM targets

===============================================================================
IV. S_ECHO — STATE IDENTITY FUNCTION
===============================================================================

Cryptographic identity binding of system state.
pub fn s_echo(&self) -> u64 {
    let mut h: u64 = 0xcbf29ce484222325;

    for i in 0..self.entities.len() {
        h ^= self.entities[i] as u64;
        h = h.wrapping_mul(1099511628211);

        h ^= self.pos[i].0 as u64;
        h = h.wrapping_mul(1099511628211);

        h ^= self.pos[i].1 as u64;
        h = h.wrapping_mul(1099511628211);
    }

    h
}
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RULE

S_ECHO(A) == S_ECHO(B) ⇒ A ≡ B

Hash = identity, not checksum.

