## DESIGN PHILOSOPHY

DVSM is partitioned into two formally distinct execution regimes:

### CORE SYSTEM (L1–L5)
- Real-time deterministic simulation kernel
- Designed for performance, predictability, and portability
- Required for all deployments

### FORENSIC EXTENSIONS (L7–L9)
- Optional high-assurance verification manifold
- Designed for auditability, integrity enforcement, and drift detection
- Activated only in high-trust / high-stakes environments

This separation ensures:
- Minimal runtime overhead for standard simulation use cases
- Maximum verification depth for regulated or adversarial environments

===============================================================================
I. CORE EXECUTION MANIFOLD (L1–L5)
===============================================================================

## L1 — Ξ EXECUTION KERNEL
Deterministic ECS update system

    S(t+1) = Ξ(S(t), I(t))

Guarantee:
- Bitwise deterministic across all platforms
- Fixed-point arithmetic (no floating drift)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## L3 — TOTAL ORDER BROADCAST
Global deterministic input sequencing

Guarantee:
- All nodes process identical command ordering
- Eliminates concurrency nondeterminism

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## L4 — STATE IDENTITY (S_ECHO)
Canonical state fingerprinting system

Guarantee:
- Each state maps to a unique deterministic identity hash

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## L5 — CONSENSUS ATTRACTOR ENGINE
Distributed finality system

Guarantee:
- State is accepted only if convergence stability is achieved
- Rejects divergent or unstable trajectories

===============================================================================
CORE TRUTH MODEL
===============================================================================

Core correctness is binary:

    S_A == S_B  ⇔  S_ECHO(A) == S_ECHO(B)

This defines:

- Execution correctness
- Replay correctness
- Consensus correctness

===============================================================================
II. FORENSIC MANIFOLD EXTENSIONS (L7–L9)
===============================================================================

These layers are OPTIONAL, COMPOSABLE, and AUDIT-FOCUSED.

They do NOT modify core execution semantics.

They operate as independent verification overlays.

===============================================================================
L7 — HOLLOW MERKLE (SUB-MANIFOLD VERIFICATION)
===============================================================================

## TYPE
Optional Partial State Attestation Layer

## PURPOSE
Enable verification of localized ECS regions without requiring full-state reconstruction.

## FORMAL MODEL

    H(S) = MerkleRoot(Leaf_1 ... Leaf_n)

## FUNCTIONAL ROLE
- Region-based validation (interest management)
- Sharded simulation trust boundaries
- Partial proof-of-state systems

## SYSTEM PROPERTY
Transforms DVSM from:
    "global state verification"
into:
    "localized verifiable sub-state systems"

## CLASSIFICATION
Add-on: High-Scale Distributed Optimization Layer

===============================================================================
L8 — TOPOLOGY GUARD (STRUCTURAL INVARIANCE LAYER)
===============================================================================

## TYPE
Optional Structural Integrity Enforcement Layer

## PURPOSE
Validate ECS graph integrity independently of simulation values

## FORMAL CONSTRAINT

    T(S_t) ≅ T(S_{t+1}) mod ΔC

## FUNCTIONAL ROLE
- Detects entity corruption
- Prevents ghost injection
- Ensures ECS layout consistency

## SYSTEM PROPERTY
Separates:
- VALUE correctness (L1–L5)
from
- STRUCTURE correctness (L8)

## CLASSIFICATION
Add-on: Security & Memory Integrity Layer

===============================================================================
L9 — SPECTRAL MONITOR (FORENSIC DRIFT DETECTOR)
===============================================================================

## TYPE
Optional Temporal Stability & Forensic Analysis Layer

## PURPOSE
Detect latent nondeterminism before it manifests as consensus failure

## FORMAL MODEL

    Spec(S) = FFT(ΔS_ECHO)

## FUNCTIONAL ROLE
- Detects bit-flip instability trends
- Identifies hardware-level drift
- Provides predictive failure analysis

## SYSTEM PROPERTY
Transforms system monitoring from:
    reactive failure detection
into:
    predictive stability forecasting

## CLASSIFICATION
Add-on: Forensic & Reliability Engineering Layer

===============================================================================
III. CORE VS FORENSIC SEPARATION MODEL
===============================================================================

## CORE SYSTEM (MANDATORY)
- L1 Execution Kernel
- L3 Ordering Engine
- L4 Identity Layer
- L5 Consensus Engine

PROPERTY:
- Minimal latency
- Deterministic execution
- Real-time simulation

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## FORENSIC SYSTEM (OPTIONAL)
- L7 Partial Verification
- L8 Structural Integrity
- L9 Spectral Stability

PROPERTY:
- Audit-grade verification
- Post-hoc or parallel execution
- High computational cost acceptable

===============================================================================
IV. TRUTH MODEL TRANSFORMATION
===============================================================================

## CORE MODEL (L1–L5)

Truth is binary:

    TRUE ⇔ S_A == S_B

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## EXTENDED MODEL (L1–L9)

Truth becomes convergent:

    TRUE ⇔
        structural_integrity(S) ∧
        spectral_stability(S) ∧
        identity_consistency(S)

===============================================================================
V. ARCHITECTURAL GUARANTEE SHIFT
===============================================================================

## WITHOUT FORENSICS
- System guarantees correctness of execution

## WITH FORENSICS (L7–L9)
- System guarantees correctness of:
  - execution (L1–L5)
  - structure (L8)
  - sub-state integrity (L7)
  - temporal stability (L9)

===============================================================================
VI. DEPLOYMENT MODES
===============================================================================

### MODE 1 — STANDARD SIMULATION
Enabled:
- L1–L5 only

Use case:
- Games
- Real-time simulation
- Low-latency systems

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### MODE 2 — FORENSIC VERIFIED SIMULATION
Enabled:
- L1–L9 full stack

Use case:
- Finance
- Competitive integrity systems
- Distributed verification systems
- High-assurance simulation environments

===============================================================================
VII. FINAL DESIGN PRINCIPLE
===============================================================================

DVSM separates computation into:

    EXECUTION (what happens)
    STRUCTURE (what exists)
    STABILITY (how it evolves)

Only when all three agree is reality considered valid.

