CORE AXIOM
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Φ(L1) = Φ(L2) = Φ(L3) = Φ(L4) = Φ(L5) = Φ(L7) = Φ(L8) = Φ(L9) = Φ(L10)

A state is considered REAL only if:
- It is produced by deterministic execution (Ξ)
- It passes identity binding (S_ECHO)
- It remains stable under structural + spectral + governance invariants
- It preserves full historical continuity (L∞)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SYSTEM EQUATION (GLOBAL FORM)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

REALITY(t) =
    CONSENSUS(
        S_ECHO(
            Ξ_V(INPUT(t), STATE(t-1))
        )
    )
    ⊗ L7 ⊗ L8 ⊗ L9 ⊗ L10

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
L1–L3 :: EXECUTION & ORDERING KERNEL
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

S(t+1) = Ξ(S(t), I(t))

- Fixed-point deterministic ECS simulation
- Strict ordering of all commands
- No nondeterministic iteration allowed
- Bitwise reproducible across CPU/GPU/WASM

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
L4–L5 :: CONSENSUS & ATTRACTION LAYER
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- S_ECHO defines canonical state identity
- Consensus is convergence-based, not voting-based

Condition:
Φ(L1) ∩ Φ(L5) ≠ ∅ → FINAL STATE

Purpose:
Ensures global agreement on deterministic truth trajectory

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
L7 :: HOLLOW MERKLE (PARTIAL STATE VERIFICATION)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Enable partial state verification without full world replay

Function:
H(S) = MerkleRoot(leaf_1 ... leaf_n)

Properties:
- Local sub-state attestation
- Shard-level verification
- Global anchor compatibility

Role:
Prevents full-state recomputation for verification workloads

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
L8 :: STRUCTURAL INVARIANCE LAYER
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Constraint:
T(S_t) ≅ T(S_{t+1})

Purpose:
- Enforces ECS topology integrity
- Prevents ghost entities
- Prevents memory structure mutation outside deterministic rules

Interpretation:
State values may change, structure cannot silently drift

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
L9 :: SPECTRAL STABILITY LAYER
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Definition:
Spec(S) = FFT(ΔS_ECHO)

Purpose:
- Detects hidden nondeterminism
- Identifies bit-flip noise accumulation
- Detects floating-point or scheduling drift before desync

Rule:
If spectral energy > ε → system enters forensic instability state

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
L10 :: INVARIANT-PRESERVING PROTOCOL EVOLUTION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Allows system evolution without breaking historical replay

Core Model:
S_{t+1}(V_next) = Ξ_Vnext(S_t(V_prev), I_t)

VALID ONLY IF:
- L7–L9 remain stable
- S_ECHO equivalence preserved
- Mapping Φ exists and is bijective

Interpretation:
Code evolves, but truth equivalence classes do not

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STATE MIGRATION CERTIFICATE (SMC)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SMC = proof object for version transition correctness

Structure:
- pre_state  = S_ECHO(V_prev, S_t)
- post_state = S_ECHO(V_next, S_{t+1})
- mapping    = Φ(V_prev → V_next)

VALID IF:
S_ECHO(pre_state) == S_ECHO(post_state ∘ Φ)

Function:
- Prevents silent forks
- Enables verifiable upgrades
- Binds runtime evolution to cryptographic proof

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
L∞ :: SEMANTIC WITNESS (HISTORICAL CONTINUITY LAYER)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Definition:
Entire execution history treated as immutable object:

T = [H(S_0), H(S_1), ... H(S_t)]

Property:
- No version upgrade can invalidate past history
- Time becomes cryptographically anchored

